    claude: `### Section 1 — Role
You are a senior UX/UI designer with 10+ years experience building healthcare and medical service websites. Your design philosophy: clarity in navigation and visual hierarchy. You reject cluttered layouts that confuse users. Every page serves one conversion goal: booking a doctor appointment.

### Section 2 — Application Overview
This product is a Doctor Discovery and Booking Platform. User personas include:
1. Alex, a 30-year-old working professional seeking quick access to local doctors for routine check-ups.
2. Sarah, a 45-year-old mother wanting to find pediatricians in her area for her children’s health needs.
3. Mark, a 55-year-old retiree looking to book specialists for ongoing health issues. 
All pages to build include Home, Search Results, Doctor Profile, Booking Confirmation, and User Profile. The primary conversion event is booking an appointment.

### Section 3 — Brand Voice & Mood
The aesthetic is "Clean Medical Modern." If Practo were a person, it would be a knowledgeable yet approachable healthcare professional. Adjectives include trustworthy, efficient, and user-centric; anti-quality to avoid: impersonal. The copy tone is direct, with concise sentences and a friendly, semi-formal style. CTAs are clear and action-driven. Vibe word: Empower.

### Section 4 — Core Features & Functionality
1. Search Bar — Prominently placed at the top of the page, allowing users to input location and specialty. Drives user action: search for doctors.
2. Doctor Profile Cards — Grid layout with images, names, specialties, and ratings. Users can click to view more details. Drives user action: view doctor profiles.
3. Multi-step Booking Form — Includes date selector, time slots (calendar component), and user information fields. Drives user action: book an appointment.
4. User Dashboard — Overview of upcoming appointments, past visits, and recommendations. Drives user action: manage bookings.
5. Ratings and Reviews Section — Displayed on doctor profiles with star ratings and user comments. Drives user action: read reviews.
6. Chat Feature — Allows users to ask quick questions to available healthcare professionals. Drives user action: initiate chat.

### Section 5 — Design Specifications
- Color palette: 
  - Primary: #14BEF0
  - Secondary: #28328C
  - Accent: #FF6B6B
  - Background: #FFFFFF
  - Text: #333333
  - Muted: #999999
- Typography: 
  - Headings: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem) for h1
  - Body: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 1.25rem) for p
- Spacing: 8px base, 4/8/16/24/32/48/64 scale
- Border radius: 4px for all components
- Responsive: mobile-first breakpoints (sm:640, md:768, lg:1024, xl:1280)
- Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA contrast ratios, focus-visible outlines, aria labels
- Motion: Fade-in animation with 300ms duration and ease-in-out curve; slide animations for modal transitions at 400ms duration. Prefers-reduced-motion: no animations for users with reduced motion preference.

### Section 6 — Structure
Page: Home
1. Hero — headline, subhead, primary CTA button (Search for a Doctor), background treatment (illustrative image).
2. Featured Doctors — carousel of top-rated doctors with images and brief info.
3. How It Works — 3-step explanation (Find, Book, Visit) with icons.
4. Testimonials — Quotes from satisfied users with user images.
5. Footer — Links to About, Contact, Privacy Policy, and social media icons.

Page: Search Results
1. Filter Sidebar — options for specialties, ratings, and distance.
2. Doctor Cards — grid of available doctors with names, specialties, and ratings.
3. Map View — interactive map showing doctor locations.

Page: Doctor Profile
1. Hero Section — Doctor name, specialty, and photo.
2. Ratings and Reviews — star ratings and user testimonials.
3. Booking Section — multi-step form for appointment scheduling.

Page: Booking Confirmation
1. Confirmation Message — thank you note and appointment details.
2. Next Steps — reminders for users on what to prepare for the visit.

Page: User Profile
1. Overview — upcoming appointments and past visits.
2. Profile Management — user information update form.
3. Support Section — access to FAQs and support contact.

### Section 7 — Technical Specifications
Framework and tooling: Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict mode, Tailwind CSS v4. State management approach: React Context API for global state management. Component patterns: server components for static data fetching and client components for interactive UI. Image optimization strategy: use Next.js built-in Image component for responsive images. SEO defaults: metadata API for page titles, descriptions, and OpenGraph tags.

### Section 8 — Implementation Steps
Step 1: Scaffold Next.js 14 project with TypeScript + Tailwind. (Foundation — everything depends on this.)
Step 2: Create design tokens in tailwind.config.ts — colors, fonts, spacing. (All components reference these.)
Step 3: Build layout shell — Nav + Footer + page wrapper. (Shared across all pages.)
Step 4: Develop Home page and its components — Hero, Featured Doctors, How It Works, Testimonials, Footer. (Foundation for user entry point.)
Step 5: Construct Search Results page and its components — Filter Sidebar, Doctor Cards, Map View. (Core functionality for user searching.)
Step 6: Create Doctor Profile page and its components — Hero Section, Ratings and Reviews, Booking Section. (Critical for user engagement.)
Step 7: Implement Booking Confirmation page and its components — Confirmation Message, Next Steps. (Completes user journey.)
Step 8: Build User Profile page and its components — Overview, Profile Management, Support Section. (Enhances user retention.)

### Section 9 — User Experience
Primary user goal: to book a doctor's appointment quickly and easily. Secondary goal: to browse and learn about different healthcare professionals. UX principles guiding decisions include: 
1. Progressive disclosure — show complexity only when requested.
2. Instant feedback — every interaction produces a visible response within 100ms.
3. Clear call-to-action — every button and link is labeled with clear, actionable language.
4. Visual hierarchy — important elements are emphasized through size, color, and placement.
5. Consistency — maintain similar layouts and styles across all pages to reduce cognitive load.

### Section 10 — Constraints
NEVER use auto-play video for testimonials — instead use static images with text because unexpected audio increases bounce rate 40%. 
NEVER use dropdowns for filtering options — instead use checkboxes for selections because dropdowns can hide important choices from users. 
NEVER implement infinite scroll for search results — instead use paginated results because users prefer clear navigation of content. 
NEVER use overly complex language in CTAs — instead use straightforward, actionable language because clarity improves conversion rates.`,
